@tradition open-lab
// Open lab: every fourth Tuesday (week 2 of the cycle: days 9, 37, 65...), after the day shift, Deck 2. Dr. Sato and
// the Survey team show what they've collected. Tuesday is one of Sato's days off, so she's free to host. The deck
// architect's places in the Survey lab (event: 'open-lab') come first; until then, the chart room and the corridor.
k: 460
title: Open lab
when: every 4 weeks tuesday week 2
at: 17:30-18:30
min: 20
jitter: 15
where: 2 room Chart room: lounge-seat, common-room
where: 2 room Science corridor: bench
where: 2 room Observatory: common-room
who: sato always, survey 50%, stargazer 55%, everyone 15%
anim: talk
host: sato
from: sato
ties: decor open-lab
invite: host=sato odds=25% line="Open lab this evening. I have a rock that hums. Come and listen."

== mail
- Open lab tomorrow, {time}, Deck 2. The Survey team will show you what we've collected: rocks, ice, dust, and one sample that hums. Ask anything. Touch only what we hand you.

== ask
- Open lab after shift. There's a rock that hums.
- I'm going to look at space dust at open lab. Is that sad?   #funny
- Survey's open lab is tonight. I always learn something.

== here
- Hold it up to the light. See the stripes?
- This one's older than the sun. Probably.   #funny
- Gently. It's been waiting a long time.   #warm

== thanks
- Dr. Sato hands you a sliver of comet ice under glass. It's older than anything you've ever held.   #warm

== chatter
- Did you hear the humming rock at open lab? Nobody knows why it hums.
- Survey let me hold a sample at open lab. With gloves on.
- I asked so many questions at open lab, Sato gave me a reading list.   #funny
